# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 1 — Q5's one-difference control.
#
# Byte-for-byte `q5_guard_must_be_callsite_scoped.ebnf` with the `&"a"` guard removed, so
# the ONLY difference between the two files is the guard. Without it the star is free to
# consume the whole run and the parse completes.
#
# REQUIRED VERDICT: ACCEPT on "aaa".
#
# Without this arm, Q5's REJECT would not be attributable to the guard — it could be any
# property of the two-rule shape. With it, the pair isolates the guard and nothing else.
@entry: true
scratch := star_rule
star_rule := ( "a" )*
